<!-- CONVERTED — VISUALLY VERIFIED --><chapter xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude" xml:id="ch16-power-series-taylor-polynomials-and-taylor-series">
  <title>Power Series, Taylor Polynomials, and Taylor Series</title>
  <shorttitle>Power Series and Taylor Series</shorttitle>

  <introduction><p>A power series has terms of the form <m>c_n(x-a)^n</m>, with fixed coefficients <m>c_n</m> and center <m>a</m>. We will determine where it converges and justify algebra and calculus with it strictly inside its radius of convergence. Taylor polynomials match derivatives at a chosen point; remainder estimates determine whether they approximate the function and whether its Taylor series represents it.</p></introduction>

